# 7.2 mainline kernel for the Google Pixel 2 / 2 XL (MSM8998), built from
# pristine kernel.org v7.2.2 plus a numbered series, per the pmaports convention
# that a device kernel pins a release artifact rather than the tip of a fork.
#
# Rebased from the -6.18 aport on 2026-08-28. Of that series' 188 patches, 150
# applied to v7.2 untouched, 16 needed a conflict resolved and 10 were dropped
# because upstream now carries them:
#
#   0049  dpu: upstream reworked the same wait_for_commit_done() condition into
#         the De Morgan of ours
#   0121  drm/msm shrinker deadlock -- was a backport, now in-tree
#   0122  drm/msm forbid mem reclaim from reset -- likewise
#   0123  drm/msm: always recover the gpu -- likewise
#   0124-0127, 0130  five ath10k fixes -- likewise
#   0157  irq-qcom-mpm mbox_client_txdone() -- upstream calls it now
#
# Five 6.18->7.2 API changes were folded into the commits that introduce the
# code, so the series stays bisectable:
#   snd_soc_kcontrol_component() -> snd_kcontrol_chip()          (tas2557)
#   snd_soc_dapm_kcontrol_dapm() -> snd_soc_dapm_kcontrol_to_dapm() (q6routing)
#   .pcm_construct -> .pcm_new                                    (q6voice-dai)
#   apr callbacks take a const apr_resp_pkt                       (q6voice, -dbg)
#   drm_panel_init() is static -- devm_drm_panel_alloc() instead  (sw43402)
#   qcom_ep_reset_{assert,deassert}() -> qcom_pcie_perst_*()      (pcie-qcom)
#   camss regulators[] is struct regulator_bulk_data, not char *  (camss 8998)
# 0020 also moves qrtr_device_id into include/linux/device-id/qrtr.h, following
# the treewide mod_devicetable.h split.
#
# CONFIG_BOOTPARAM_SOFTLOCKUP_PANIC and CONFIG_BOOTPARAM_HUNG_TASK_PANIC became
# int (default 0) upstream. `olddefconfig` on the 6.18 config therefore turns
# both panic-on-hang nets OFF without saying so. They are set to 1 here. Check
# them after any config regeneration.
#
# The series is the kernel this port is measured on: 11 generic msm8998 fixes
# that were only in the msm8998-mainline fork, the device bring-up patches, and
# the fixes that follow them (camera write path, audio/SLIMbus/APR, IPA,
# CPRh/OSM cpufreq, display, sensors, radios).
#
# NOTE: renumbered by the rebase. 0090/0091 carry the osm_setup_stop and
# cprh_init_stop module params, and 0119 sets their defaults. Their default of
# 0 is a safety gate, not a debug knob left on by accident: programming the
# OSM/CPRh sequence unconditionally hangs MSM8998 with no console output (see
# qcom-cpufreq-hw.c, cpr3.c and
# docs/campaign/KERNEL-BASE-RECONCILIATION.md D.0-D.6 upstream). A prior
# rebase dropped them as "[BRINGUP] instrumentation" -- do not do that again
# without first proving the sequence is safe.
#
# 0161 is BRINGUP scaffolding and must be dropped before this series is
# published, together with CONFIG_SND_SOC_QDSP6_VOICE_DBG. It is a debugfs pipe
# to the ADSP voice services, and it exists only until a real q6voice driver is
# written -- see docs/CALL-AUDIO-2026-08-25.md for the specification it
# measured. (The -6.18 aport's header called this 0175; that number had already
# drifted to the q6routing patch, which stays.)
#
# Kernel config based on: taimen_defconfig
